# SENIM — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your Supabase project credentials.
# Get these from: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
#
# The variable names MUST match exactly what supabase.ts reads (see src/lib/supabase.ts).

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo seed / reset (server-side scripts only — NEVER expose in the frontend)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are read by `npm run demo:seed` and `npm run demo:reset`
# (scripts/demo-seed.mjs, scripts/demo-reset.mjs). They are NOT prefixed with
# VITE_, so Vite never bundles them into the client.
#
# Local Supabase: run `supabase status` to get the service_role key.
# Cloud Supabase: Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role.
#
# SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key